Table~\ref{tab:temporal_alignment} complements the main article's retained synchronization plot with lag-estimation error, exact-lag accuracy, and activation rate across all eleven offsets. All three conditions use the fixed central 20-frame interval, and the confidence threshold was selected on validation data. Correction helps positive delays but worsens negative integer leads; its 41.5\% activation rate at zero offset shows that the procedure can introduce unnecessary corrections. This diagnostic is not part of the main fusion method.
